, please avoid double posting, as it is against the forum rules. You can use the "Edit" function on your posts to add additional information you've forgotten or respond to multiple people. You can review our forum rules
here
. Thank you.
Dehsalp said:
However, wasn't that based on probability? Also, I understood that it only blocked damage when an ally's HP was low. Furthermore, it did not block skills other than the opponent's 'normal attacks' (especially area-of-effect skills and those that select random targets).
Click to expand...
Substitute isnt based on probability. It'll always happen if the conditions are met. the engine's default conditions are that the tank has a substitute trait on them (state, equipment, w/e), the target of the attack is dying (below 25% of their max hp), and the attack is not a certain hit (must be either physical or magical). The scope of the attack does not matter. If this isnt the case, then you may have a plugin interfering.
Dehsalp said:
However, since I am a layman when it comes to coding or JavaScript... I was unable to write the code myself. I was also already using Yanfly's Buffs and States Core plugin.
Click to expand...
are you also using the aura plugin? it'd simplify the party guard a bit by letting you tie that entire effect on all other party into one visible state on the tank and automatically ends it if the tank loses their state.
Dehsalp said:
1. A - When used, protects a 'specific' ally. This guard takes all damage from the designated ally instead. (I want to create skills that last for 1 turn, multiple turns, or even indefinitely from the start of combat.)
Click to expand...
a basic form of it could be:
Code:
<Custom React Effect>
if (this.isForOpponent() && this.isDamage() && target != origin && origin.isAlive()){
   const rate = 1;
   const dmg = Math.ceil(value * rate);
   value = Math.max(0, value - dmg);

   origin.gainHp(-dmg);
   origin.startDamagePopup();
   if (origin.hp === 0 && !origin.isStateResist(1))
        origin.performCollapse();
}

if (origin.isDead()){
  target.removeState(stateId);
}
</Custom React Effect>

<Custom Remove Effect>
user.friendsUnit().aliveMembers().forEach(m=> {
   if (user != m && m.isStateAffected(stateId) && m.stateOrigin(stateId) === user.stateOrigin(stateId))
      m.removeState(stateId);
})
</Custom Remove Effect>
where the tank gives the state to an ally and the state reduces a portion of the damage and redirects it to the tank. All you'd need to do is change the "rate" variable to the percentage of the damage the tank should take.
Dehsalp said:
2. B - When used, protects all allies for n turns and takes damage on their behalf.
3. C - When used, this guard takes 'partial' damage on their behalf for n turns.
Click to expand...
same as above, but the skill that applies this state targets all allies and you change the rate variable accordingly (.5 = 50%, 1.5 = 150%, etc).
As mentioned, the aura plugin can make it so that a state thats placed on the tank can project the protection state on all allies and that'd handle the durations and removing the state from the others should the tank die, but it's not required. It'd also need a slight readjustment for the code, but you havent mentioned using it yet.
the remove effect should remove the protection from all allies if the tank dies from protecting someone else, and the state removes itself from the target (and then all allies) if the target takes a hit while the tank is dead, but I haven't tried that out to make sure it covers all situations.

