Oh, I apologize. I remember answering that way when I used the forum a few years ago. I will be more careful and keep that in mind from now on.
Yes, that is correct. The problem was the condition of 'low HP,' meaning protecting allies with less than 25% HP. In my case, attacks from some bosses (like those on challenging difficulty or hidden bosses) are very powerful from the start, so I could die even with 100% HP; therefore, what I had previously was useless.
I had considered adding an Aura plugin before, but decided against it because it wasn't really necessary.
Not all skills need to be in the form of an 'Aura,' but is an Aura plugin absolutely necessary for using the <Custom React Effect> you mentioned? I intend to avoid adding plugins as much as possible in the current state.
Additionally, there is another reason why I do not want to include it as an Aura.
First, since I was just giving an example, it doesn't actually need to last infinitely. I am already using passive and buff & state plugins, and I believe I can make it last from the start by not specifying the duration of the state turns. Another reason is that this buff actually needs to last only for a 'small number of turns' at the 'desired timing'. (Of course, it seems like this could be resolved by using a skill to add just a few turns to the state.)
This is what I have written so far based on my understanding, but please verify if my understanding of the code you provided below is correct.
Code:
