Do I only need to modify the part `const rate = 'N'` in the code you wrote?
The part below that, `const dmg = Math.ceil(value * rate);`, appears to be retrieving the value set by the 'rate' just above it. Is that correct?
In other words, if I use it exactly as you wrote, 1 = 100%.
This means the Guard takes 100% of the damage received by the ally. Is that correct?
If I set this value to 0.5, does that mean the protected ally's HP takes 50% of the damage, and the Guard takes the remaining 50%? Or does it fully defend the allies' health while dealing 50% of the damage to the guards?
Additionally, in the case of 1.5, is it correct that it blocks all damage to allies, and the guards take 150% of that damage—in other words, the guards take an additional 50% of the damage?
If so, to utilize this,
I create a skill named 'A' for the 'Guard' and set its target to 'Allies'.
I insert a state named 'S', which has the code above entered into this skill 'A'.
The Guard uses skill A on an ally.
Is that correct?
